    "body": "Here would be my attempt:\r\n\r\n> Reflection is primarily about improving web developer ergonomics by giving them typed access to content attributes through reflected IDL attributes. The ultimate source of truth, which the rest of the web platform specification ecosystem interacts with, is still the content attributes themselves. That is, specification authors must not use the reflected IDL attribute's getter or setter steps, but instead must use the content attribute's presence and value. (Or some appropriate abstraction on top of it, such as the current state of an [enumerated attribute].)",
